; Regression test for issue #3261: a C directive that equated a commodity
; with the null commodity merged the two, and reports showed the commodity's
; amounts without its symbol or number format, whichever side the bare
; number was written on.  The null commodity is not a unit, so a conversion
; must name a commodity on each side; anything else is rejected in place.

C 1 "" = 1 $
C 1 $ = 1 ""
C 1,00 PLN = 1,00
C 1 "" = 1 ""

2021-01-01 Test
    A               $10
    B

test bal -> 4
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 7:
Error: Commodity conversion requires a commodity on each side
While parsing file "$FILE", line 8:
Error: Commodity conversion requires a commodity on each side
While parsing file "$FILE", line 9:
Error: Commodity conversion requires a commodity on each side
While parsing file "$FILE", line 10:
Error: Commodity conversion requires a commodity on each side
end test
